axes.runtime:
Official hosted remote server (https://mcp.firecrawl.dev/v2/mcp) + local npx (firecrawl-mcp), two lines;
the official README states support for both cloud and self-hosted. GitHub 7,673★, last push 2026-10-23 (API verified);
the release line lives on npm (firecrawl-mcp 3.34.1), GitHub releases stopped at v3.2.1 (2025-09-26) — behind npm.

axes.fit:
Fits: agents that want the full chain covered in one package — "search→fetch text→structured JSON→browser interaction→site-level crawl/map→page monitoring";
gradual onboarding that starts keyless and upgrades to a key.
Not a fit: holding a browser session long-term and driving it step by step (the README states plainly this is not its interaction model);
minimal scenarios that only need single-page reading (the fetch reference is lighter).
